tool_input.prompt:
Create a separate VS Code extension at `semio/vscode/` that opens kit.json files in a sketchpad webview editor. Also revert the KitEditorProvider that was incorrectly added to `repo/vscode/`.

## Context
- There is an empty file at `/workspaces/semio/semio/vscode/extensio.ts` (note: typo in filename, this was created by the user)
- The repo/vscode extension at `/workspaces/semio/repo/vscode/` was incorrectly modified to include a `KitEditorProvider` and customEditors contribution — these need to be reverted
- The existing repo/vscode extension uses Vite to build a CJS bundle for VS Code
- The sketchpad builds to `semio/sketchpad/dist/`

## Tasks

### Part A: Create semio/vscode extension

#### 1. Rename `extensio.ts` to `extension.ts`
Run: `mv /workspaces/semio/semio/vscode/extensio.ts /workspaces/semio/semio/vscode/extension.ts`

#### 2. Write `/workspaces/semio/semio/vscode/extension.ts`
This VS Code extension provides a custom editor for kit.json files. Follow the same patterns as `repo/vscode/extension.ts`.

```typescript
// #region 🔖Header
// [👤semio🖱️vscode💻extension](semiorepo://p/u/semio/b/u/vscode/f/extension.ts)

// 2026 Ueli Saluz <ueli@semio-tech.com>

// This program is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify
